Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [configuration]

Disable the Ghostty resize overlay by default. On GNOME/Wayland, the resize
overlay triggers an infinite resize feedback loop with Mutter/compositor
configure events, causing continuous flickering and freezing window input.
GNOME applications do not show resize overlays by convention. Users can still
explicitly enable it via `resize-overlay = after-first` or `always` in their
config file.

--- a/src/config/Config.zig
+++ b/src/config/Config.zig
@@ -2277,5 +2277,5 @@ pub const Config = struct {
 ///                     subsequently resized.
 ///
-/// The default is `after-first`.
-@"resize-overlay": ResizeOverlay = .@"after-first",
+/// The default is `never`.
+@"resize-overlay": ResizeOverlay = .never,
 
